IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-art24-25-powers`
IMPORT `g7-art37-43-final`

-- g7-tests-powers-final: Articles 24, 25 and 37 to 43.  Expected values were decided from the text before the run:
--   24(2): the relevant terms are “charitable”, “public benefit” and any related term OTHER THAN “charity” that the Regulations specify.
--   24(1): the power reaches the use of a relevant term, other than by a registered charity, in relation to soliciting donations from the general public or from a prescribed description of persons.
--   24(4): an offence created by the Regulations carries a penalty no greater than a fine: no imprisonment.
--   37(1): a limited liability partnership, a separate limited partnership or a body corporate; consent or connivance PROVED; a partner (of the partnership) or a director, governor, secretary or other similar officer
--          (of the body corporate), or a person purporting to act in such a capacity; liable to the penalty provided for the offence.   37(2): a member of a body corporate managed by its members is treated as a director.
--   38: no rule fixes the date of service; the reading taken is the date of receipt.   39(1): five kinds of provision, never an amendment of this Law.   41(1): three kinds of enactment.   42(b): not this Law.

§ `Articles 24, 25 and 37 to 43 — tests`

`fav` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
`other F7.6` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.6`
`other F7.7` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.7`
`other F7.10` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.10`
`other F7.13` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.13`
`other F7.14` MEANS `the interpretation with the other reading of F7.14`

§§ `Article 24 — relevant terms, the use the power reaches, and the cap on the penalty`

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`no further terms specified` MEANS EMPTY
`the Regulations specify philanthropic` MEANS LIST "philanthropic"
`the Regulations specify charity and philanthropic` MEANS LIST "charity", "philanthropic"

#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "charitable" `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "public benefit" `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "charity" `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "philanthropic" `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "philanthropic" `the Regulations specify philanthropic`
-- “other than ‘charity’”: the Regulations cannot specify “charity” as a relevant term.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "charity" `the Regulations specify charity and philanthropic`
#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "philanthropic" `the Regulations specify charity and philanthropic`
#ASSERT `Art 24(2) the term is a relevant term` "charitable" `the Regulations specify philanthropic`
#ASSERT count `the relevant terms named in Article 24(2)` EQUALS 2

GIVEN term IS A STRING
      registered IS A BOOLEAN
      soliciting IS A BOOLEAN
      public IS A BOOLEAN
      prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use of a relevant term under Article 24`
`a use of a term` term registered soliciting public prescribed MEANS
    `Use of a relevant term under Article 24` WITH
        term IS term
        `by a registered charity` IS registered
        `in relation to the soliciting of donations` IS soliciting
        `from the general public` IS public
        `from a prescribed description of persons` IS prescribed

#ASSERT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "charitable" FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "charitable" FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "charitable" TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "charitable" FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "charitable" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "charity" FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "philanthropic" FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `no further terms specified`
#ASSERT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "philanthropic" FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `the Regulations specify philanthropic`
#ASSERT `Art 24(1) the use is one that the Regulations may restrict` (`a use of a term` "public benefit" FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `no further terms specified`

`a penalty of no imprisonment and no fine` MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `no fine is provided`
`a penalty of a fine with no maximum stated` MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
`a penalty of a fine of level 3` MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3
`a penalty of one month and a fine` MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 1, fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
`a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 24, fine IS `no fine is provided`

#ASSERT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` `a penalty of a fine of level 3`
#ASSERT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` `a penalty of a fine with no maximum stated`
#ASSERT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` `a penalty of no imprisonment and no fine`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` `a penalty of one month and a fine`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24(4) the penalty is no greater than a fine` `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months`

-- F7.13: Article 24(3)(a) (adapt Articles 21 to 23, whose offences carry imprisonment) against the cap of Article 24(4) (“no greater than a fine”).  Reading taken: the cap binds every offence of the Regulations.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` TRUE `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` FALSE `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of a fine of level 3` TRUE `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of a fine of level 3` FALSE `fav`
-- Other reading: an offence adapted from Articles 21 to 23 may keep its imprisonment; an offence not so adapted is still capped.
#ASSERT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` TRUE `other F7.13`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` FALSE `other F7.13`
#ASSERT `Art 24 the Regulations may attach this penalty to the offence` `a penalty of a fine of level 3` FALSE `other F7.13`

§§ `Article 25 — the illustrative content of an Order is carried as text and no rule reads it`

#ASSERT count `the statements that an Order under Article 25(1) may require a charity to state (Article 25(2)(a))` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT count `the other provision that an Order under Article 25(1) may make (Article 25(2)(b) to (d))` EQUALS 3

§§ `Article 37 — an officer of a body that offended`

GIVEN body IS A `Kind of body that offended under Article 37`
      offended IS A BOOLEAN
      proved IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A `Capacity of a person in relation to a body under Article 37`
      how IS A `How a person comes within a capacity under Article 37`
GIVETH A `Facts for Article 37`
`facts of Article 37` body offended proved capacity how MEANS
    `Facts for Article 37` WITH
        `kind of body` IS body
        `the body committed an offence under this Law` IS offended
        `consent or connivance is proved` IS proved
        capacity IS capacity
        `how the person comes within the capacity` IS how

-- As printed (the reading taken): partners of a limited liability partnership or a separate limited partnership; directors, governors, secretaries and similar officers of a body corporate; those purporting to act as such.
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a separate limited partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a separate limited partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a secretary of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a secretary of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `another officer similar to a director, governor or secretary of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `another officer similar to a director, governor or secretary of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a separate limited partnership` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `none of these` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
-- Not proved, or no offence by the body: not also guilty.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE FALSE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` FALSE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
-- 37(2): a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members is treated as a director (a limited liability partnership has partners, not this).
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, in connection with the member’s functions of management` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, in connection with the member’s functions of management` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 37(2) the member is treated as a director of the body corporate` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, in connection with the member’s functions of management` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(2) the member is treated as a director of the body corporate` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, in connection with the member’s functions of management` `holds the capacity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(2) the member is treated as a director of the body corporate` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`)
-- Trap T26: an unincorporated association and the trustees of a trust are entities (Article 2(1)) but are not named in 37(1): a committee member who connived is not within it as written.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `the trustees of a trust` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `the trustees of a trust` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `fav`
-- The other reading of F7.6: they are within it (their governors are officers).
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.6`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.6`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `none of these` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.6`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `the trustees of a trust` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.6`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `the trustees of a trust` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.6`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `the trustees of a trust` TRUE TRUE `none of these` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.6`
-- The other reading of F7.10: any listed capacity for any body within Article 37(1): a director of a limited liability partnership, a partner of a body corporate.
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.10`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.10`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `none of these` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.10`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `other F7.10`

-- The penalty is the body’s own, in the same manner.
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the penalty of the person who is also guilty` (`facts of Article 37` `a limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE `a partner of the partnership` `holds the capacity`) `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months` `fav` EQUALS JUST `a penalty of imprisonment alone for 24 months`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the penalty of the person who is also guilty` (`facts of Article 37` `a body corporate` TRUE TRUE `a director of the body corporate` `purports to act in the capacity`) `a penalty of a fine of level 3` `fav` EQUALS JUST `a penalty of a fine of level 3`
#ASSERT `Art 37(1) the penalty of the person who is also guilty` (`facts of Article 37` `an unincorporated association` TRUE TRUE `a governor of the body corporate` `holds the capacity`) `a penalty of a fine of level 3` `fav` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Article 38 — the date on which a notice is served (F7.7)`

GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`no Order fixes a date` MEANS NOTHING

-- Sent on 2026-06-01, received on 2026-06-03 (the discriminating case of F7.7): served on the 3rd (reading taken) or the 1st.
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 3)) `no Order fixes a date` `fav` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 3
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 3)) `no Order fixes a date` `other F7.7` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
-- A notice not yet received: on the reading taken it has not been served; on the other it was served when sent.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) NOTHING `no Order fixes a date` `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) NOTHING `no Order fixes a date` `other F7.7` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
-- An Order under Article 38 that fixes a date governs, on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 3)) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 5)) `fav` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 5
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 3)) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 5)) `other F7.7` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 5
#ASSERT `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (YMD 2026 6 1) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 6 5)) `fav` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 5

§§ `Article 39 — Regulations and Orders`

#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `transitional` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `consequential` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `incidental` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `supplementary` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `savings` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `an amendment of this Law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `transitional` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 39(1) the provision may be contained in the Order or Regulations` `an amendment of this Law` FALSE

-- F7.14: R&O.56/2025 added paragraph (ba) to Article 2(1) and amended nothing else; Article 39(1) bars an amendment of the Law from the ancillary provisions of an Order and Article 39(2) speaks of Regulations only.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 39 an Order under Article 2(2) may make a consequential amendment of another provision of the Law` `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 39 an Order under Article 2(2) may make a consequential amendment of another provision of the Law` `other F7.14`

§§ `Article 41 — relevant enactments`

#ASSERT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `the Proceeds of Crime (Supervisory Bodies) (Jersey) Law 2008`
#ASSERT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `an enactment under which the JFSC has functions`
#ASSERT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `an enactment relating to taxation`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 41(1) the enactment is a relevant enactment` `some other enactment`

§§ `Articles 40(1) and 43 — carried as text`

#ASSERT `Art 43 the short title` EQUALS "Charities (Jersey) Law 2014"
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) a rule of construction preserving the independent powers of the Attorney General, the Bailiff and the court` EQUALS "Nothing in this Law is to be read as derogating from any power or function of the Attorney General, the Bailiff, or the court, being a power or function that exists independently of this Law (under customary law or otherwise), in respect of charities or of acts for charitable purposes (whether as defined in this Law or otherwise)."

